; addline_sample_returns_to_domain: a delta that lands back in the domain is
; legal.
;
; The mirror of addline_sample_leaves_domain. Both start from values[1] = 1
; and move by one; only the direction differs, and only the result decides.
; This is the vector that fails if the check is written against the delta,
; or against its sign, rather than against the sum -- -1 is not a binary
; value, but 1 + -1 is.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; binary sample, domain {0, 1}

PUSH 1
PUSH 1
SETLINE r0       ; values[1] = 1

PUSH 1
PUSH -1
ADDLINE r0       ; 1 + -1 = 0, back inside the domain

PUSH 1
GETLINE r0
STOW r1
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r1        ; outputs[0] = 0
HALT
